# Anti-slop

This repo vendors [anti-slop](https://github.com/dmmulroy/anti-slop) at
`tools/oxlint/anti-slop/` and runs it via `pnpm lint:anti-slop`.

- Do not add `as` assertions without a preceding `SAFETY:` comment that states
  the checked invariant.
- Do not use `unknown`/`any`/`object`/`{}` dictionary values, `unknown`
  parameters (except `cause`), or `unknown` return types.
- Do not `vi.mock` / `jest.mock` modules; inject seams instead.
- Do not spread `{}` to omit optional fields; use explicit assignment after a
  narrowed check (this repo enables `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`).
- Do not chain type assertions or widen a known value and assert it back.
- Prefer `satisfies` and inference over explicit broad target types.
- Run `pnpm lint:anti-slop` on TypeScript you touch. Do not disable these
  rules or launder types to silence them.
